  <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
  <section class="pfx pfx-sec pfx-sec--paper" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pfx-eyebrow">Before you book</div>
      <h2>Power flushing in Liverpool: your questions answered</h2>

      <div class="fq">
        <details><summary>How much does a power flush cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>A power flush in Liverpool costs £350 for up to 6 radiators, £495 for 7 to 10 radiators and £650 for 11 to 15 radiators. All prices include VAT. Systems over 15 radiators are £650 plus £40 per extra radiator. A single cold radiator is £80. The price is fixed before we start.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How many radiators does a typical Liverpool house have?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>A 3 bed Liverpool terrace or semi usually has 8 to 10 radiators, which puts most homes in the £495 package. A 4 bed detached usually has 10 to 12. Count every radiator including the bathroom towel rail. If you land between two packages we quote the lower one.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>What is included in the price?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Every package includes the chemical cleaner, a full machine flush of every radiator one at a time, a full dose of corrosion inhibitor to BS 7593, radiator balancing and a written report for your boiler warranty. VAT is included. The only optional extra is a magnetic filter at £195 fitted.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do you flush microbore central heating systems?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Yes. Microbore pipework is 8mm to 10mm, much narrower than standard 15mm or 22mm pipe, and it blocks with iron oxide far more easily. It needs high flow pumps, double dosed cleaner and flow reversal to clear properly. Many engineers turn these jobs down. Microbore systems are priced at a site survey because the work varies so much between systems.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I know if I have microbore pipes?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Microbore pipe is 8mm or 10mm across, noticeably thinner than standard copper pipe. Liverpool homes built between about 1985 and 2000 are the most likely to have it, including many of the semis in Childwall, Woolton and Gateacre. Look at the pipe going into a radiator valve. If it looks thin enough to bend by hand, it is probably microbore.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Which cleaning chemical do you use?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Fernox F3 on standard cleans and Sentinel X400 on heavily sludged systems. F3 is a fast universal cleaner that does its work inside an hour. X400 is a restorer that breaks down dense sludge over time and can need up to 3 or 4 weeks circulating. We choose after we see the water, not before.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How long does a power flush take?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>A small system takes 4 to 5 hours. A standard 7 to 10 radiator system takes 5 to 7 hours. A large system takes 7 to 9 hours. Heavy sludge, microbore pipework or a blocked radiator can add time. The price does not change if it takes longer.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need a magnetic filter after a power flush?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>It is not compulsory but it is the single best way to keep the system clean afterwards. A MagnaClean Professional2 catches iron oxide before it settles in the radiators and the boiler. We fit one for £195 including VAT at the same visit. Some boiler warranties now require a filter, so it is worth checking yours.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Is a power flush always the right fix?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>No. A power flush will not repair a broken pump, a stuck valve or a failed boiler part, and it will not fix a system losing pressure through a leak. If your boiler is over 15 years old and the system is badly corroded, replacing it may make more sense than flushing it. We will tell you if that is the case.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Does a power flush cause leaks?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>It can reveal them. A flush pushes water round at speed, and a radiator already corroded to the point of failure may spring a pin hole. That radiator was going to fail anyway. We check the condition of radiators and joints before we start and we tell you honestly if we think something is at risk.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Are your prices including VAT?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Yes. Every price on this page includes VAT. Worth checking with anyone else you get a quote from, because a price quoted before VAT goes up by 20 percent when the invoice arrives.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do you cover the Wirral and St Helens?</summary><div class="fq-body"><p>Yes. We cover all Liverpool postcodes plus the Wirral, St Helens, Crosby, Formby, Bootle, Maghull, Southport, Kirkby and Huyton. Travel is included in the quoted price.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


